# ImStudium

## Orient first

```bash
imstudium context --json    # semester, today, Abgaben, Klausuren, new files, news, next steps
```

Act on `next`. If it suggests `semester start`, offer it; don't run it. If the student is signed out or sees `SESSION_EXPIRED`, ask them to run `imstudium login` themselves.

## CLI first

- Time: `today`, `week [--next]`, `stundenplan`, `holidays`
- What's new: `changes --since 7d`, `news`, `feed`, `inbox --unread`
- Due: `tasks --open`, `klausuren`
- Material: `search "<words>"` (`--archive` for past semesters), then open the cited `content.md`. Also `courseware`, `wiki`, `forum`, `files tree <course>`
- People: `people`, `sprechstunden`. Planning: `catalog search <topic> --semester "SS 2027"`
- Anything else in Stud.IP: `routes <topic>`, then `api <path> --flat`

Add `--json` when parsing. A course argument can be a title fragment, slug, number or id.

## Workspace (`~/Studium`, `IMSTUDIUM_WORKSPACE`)

- `llms.txt` is the entry point. `studium.json` (resolve folders from `course.path`), `NEW.md`, `abgaben.md`, `stundenplan.md`, `klausuren.md` and `STUDIUM.md` sit at the root.
- Each course has `COURSE.md`, `files/`, `extracted/<slug>/content.md`, `search/`, `news/`, `forum/`, `courseware/` and `wiki/`. Earlier semesters are under `archive/`.
- Refresh with `imstudium sync --extract`.

## MCP (opt-in)

The `imstudium` tool runs the same read-only commands: `{"args": ["context"]}`. It refuses writes.

## Limits

- `content.md` (pdf-inspector / AnyDoc) is not LaTeX. For formulas and diagrams, open the original in `files/`. Image-only pages are marked `_(image-only page — no text layer)_`.
- Exam dates from course text are unconfirmed; tell the student to check them in Stud.IP.

## Never

- Write to Stud.IP (`api --write`, posting, messaging, booking), or run `semester start`, `sync` or `--save`, unless the student asks for that exact action.
- Handle passwords or the session. Never paste messages, grades or classmates' names elsewhere, and never upload course material. See the `imstudium-datenschutz` skill.
